============================================================
PRACTICAL 8 - NOTIFICATIONS
============================================================

Question:
Develop an android application that asks for upper bound and
lower bound value of a range. The application should list out
prime numbers existing between specified range on screen
(utilize service running in background for searching prime
numbers). Upon completion of operation, application should
prompt the user through a notification.


-------------------- AndroidManifest.xml --------------------

<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    package="com.example.primerange">

    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.POST_NOTIFICATIONS" />

    <application
        android:allowBackup="true"
        android:label="@string/app_name"
        android:supportsRtl="true"
        android:theme="@style/Theme.PrimeRange">

        <activity
            android:name=".MainActivity"
            android:exported="true">

            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER"/>
            </intent-filter>

        </activity>

        <service
            android:name=".PrimeService"
            android:exported="false" />

    </application>
</manifest>


